⭐ 1. sequentialStream
public <T> String sequentialStream(List<T> items)
✔ Converts list elements into strings
✔ Processes them sequentially
✔ Joins them with spaces " "
Example
Input: [1, 2, 3]
Output: "1 2 3"

⭐ 2. parallelStream
public <T> String parallelStream(List<T> items)
✔ Same output as sequential
✖ But processed using parallel stream (multi-threading)
⚠️ Order is NOT guaranteed, but you converted to string and joined (order preserved because joining() collects sequentially internally).

⭐ 3. containingOdd
public Boolean containingOdd(List<Integer> items)
✔ Returns true if ANY odd number exists
Uses anyMatch

⭐ 4. onlyOdd
public Boolean onlyOdd(List<Integer> items)
✔ Returns true if ALL values are odd
Uses allMatch

⭐ 5. palindromesInList
public <T> List<T> palindromesInList(List<T> items)
✔ Returns items where
string equals its reverse
Example: "madam", "121"

⭐ 6. stringsToUpperCase
public List<String> stringsToUpperCase(List<String> items)
✔ Converts all strings to UPPERCASE

⭐ 7. duplicatesInList
public <T> List<T> duplicatesInList(List<T> items)
✔ Returns only the duplicate values
✔ Uses Collections.frequency() and distinct()
Example:
Input → [1,2,2,3,3,3]
Output → [2,3]

